@startuml
title Process - runtime to solver sequence

participant "SetupProcessStep /\nLoadDataStep" as Steps
participant "FlowConfig" as FlowConfig
participant "Flow" as Flow
participant "Binders" as Binders
participant "SimulationRunner" as Runner
participant "SolverAdapter" as Adapter
participant "Backend model" as Backend

Steps -> FlowConfig: validated [flow] section
Steps -> Flow: ensure_flow(state)\nFlow(config)
Flow -> Flow: set_config(...)\nset_parameters_from_config(...)\nset_initial_conditions(...)\nset_boundary_conditions(...)\nset_sinks_sources(...)

Steps -> Binders: apply_recharge_load_result_to_flow(...)\napply_etp_load_result_to_flow(...)\napply_*_to_flow(...)
Binders -> Flow: recharge, ETP, lakes, SFR\nbound to the process object
Steps -> Binders: apply_simulation_time_to_flow_wells(...)\napply_simulation_time_to_flow_boundary_conditions(...)
note right
  Forcings are resolved to one value
  per stress period of [simulation.time].
end note

Runner -> Adapter: validate(model, options, slot)
Runner -> Adapter: build(model, options, slot, ctx)\nthe Model is read, the slot names the folder
Adapter -> Adapter: translate the Model\nto solver inputs
Adapter --> Runner: SolverRun, built in memory
Runner -> Adapter: run(solver_run)
Adapter -> Backend: write the input files and solve
Backend --> Adapter: raw outputs
Adapter --> Runner: SolverRun, solved
@enduml
